From ea5810fb3a34a2e8d46eee022b41daf03da7f50e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stefan <46031448+StefanPetersTM@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 16:29:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] soapysdr: preserve contiguous timed TX remainder handling

CP2073-CP2082 isolated descriptor churn to partial untimed remainders after timed writes. Keep contiguous remainders in the active buffer, preserve timestamp continuity, and retain bounded default-off worker diagnostics used by the CP2047 acceptance gate. This is a POC workaround for unresolved ring/backpressure behavior.
---
 .../software/soapysdr/LiteXM2SDRDevice.hpp    |   28 +-
 .../software/soapysdr/LiteXM2SDRStreaming.cpp | 1607 ++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 1576 insertions(+), 59 deletions(-)

